## How Reply Serialization Works (Current)

The pipeline has two layers:

### Layer 1 — Schema-based fast path (`lib/schemas.js:144`)
`getSchemaSerializer(context, statusCode, contentType)` walks `context[kSchemaResponse]` (populated by `compileSchemasForSerialization` in `lib/validation.js`) and returns a compiled serializer function keyed by status code and content-type, or `false` if none matches.

### Layer 2 — JSON fallback (`lib/reply.js:1018`)
```js
// lib/reply.js:1018-1024
function serialize (context, data, statusCode, contentType) {
  const fnSerialize = getSchemaSerializer(context, statusCode, contentType)
  if (fnSerialize) {
    return fnSerialize(data)      // schema-compiled serializer wins
  }
  return JSON.stringify(data)    // ← JSON fallback for everything else
}
```

