### Two Attack Vectors Covered

1. **`__proto__` injection** — e.g. `{ "__proto__": { "admin": true } }` — controlled by `onProtoPoisoning`
2. **Constructor poisoning** — e.g. `{ "constructor": { "prototype": { "foo": "bar" } } }` — controlled by `onConstructorPoisoning` (also the default `"error"` in v3, as confirmed in `test/proto-poisoning.test.js` line 77)

### Bonus: Parser Storage Also Hardened

Even the internal parser registry uses `Map` instead of a plain object (comment at line 34): *"using a map instead of a plain object to avoid prototype hijack attacks"* — so an attacker can't poison the parser lookup table either.
